# 🔢 Math Vulnerabilities

## 1. Integer Overflow/Underflow

### Pre-Solidity 0.8 (No Built-in Protection)

```solidity
// VULNERABLE (Solidity < 0.8)
uint256 balance = 0;
balance -= 1;  // Underflows to 2^256 - 1

uint8 small = 255;
small += 1;  // Overflows to 0

// MITIGATION: Use SafeMath library
using SafeMath for uint256;
balance = balance.sub(1);  // Reverts on underflow
```

### Solidity 0.8+ with Unchecked Blocks

```solidity
// VULNERABLE - unchecked bypasses protection
function dangerous(uint256 a, uint256 b) external pure returns (uint256) {
    unchecked {
        return a - b;  // Can underflow!
    }
}

// SECURE - only use unchecked when provably safe
function safe(uint256 i) external pure returns (uint256) {
    unchecked {
        return i + 1;  // Safe if i is bounded by loop
    }
}
```

