## Audit Checklist for Math Issues

- [ ] Are all arithmetic operations checked for overflow/underflow?
- [ ] Is `unchecked` used only where provably safe?
- [ ] Is multiplication done before division?
- [ ] Are rounding directions favorable to the protocol?
- [ ] Are type casts validated (especially signed→unsigned)?
- [ ] Are all divisions protected against zero divisors?
- [ ] Are decimal differences between tokens handled correctly?
- [ ] Is the first depositor attack mitigated in vaults/pools?
- [ ] Are basis points vs percentages used consistently?
- [ ] Can accumulators overflow over the contract lifetime?
